{
  "note": "gains-bundle-1110 (Rodney, Tue night 11-10): one bundle on vs off of four built, default-off gains on the combined pair master1108 (ts3native 0.36.211, ts3fixes master1108 + kWakeHooks, ts3agent from the pair): wakepark + wakepoll (docs/211, WakePark.cs), unseenpark (docs/243 §9, UnseenThrottle.cs, hook rides AutShadow's AutonomyManager.Add patch, so [AutShadow] Mode=1 and autshadow stay on in both arms as in final-bundle), Mint sub-run fusion ([MintFuse] Sub=1, docs/139 §4.4/4.6, F4). Mint fusion acts at transform time (no in-load A/B), so the whole bundle is a cross-load ABBA per world: off, on, on, off, BP then IP, 10 min, noise check on (default), seed 12345, 8 jobs. Off arm: all three runtime switches off, Sub=0. On arm: fixesOn wakepark,wakepoll,unseenpark + Sub=1. Both arms: the same package (kWakeHooks puts the per-SimUpdate-pass hook in both, the off arm pays it), same ini otherwise (final-bundle off ini: UnseenRootMotion Mode=0, repo defaults). PACKAGE TO BUILD before the run: game-copy/ts3fixes.package.master1108-wakehooks = node tools/build-fixes.ts --on kWakeHooks from master 896c0e8b/4a4a04fd (register in builds.json; ts3fixes.package.master1108 has kWakeHooks=false). Household: wake*, unseenpark use UfWhy==0 (never the active household or a selectable Sim) and the wake parks wake all on view change; unseenpark also exempts service/role/pregnant/situation Sims and lets anything doubtful through. Throttles judged by per-arm ms/s: node tools/harness/arm-ms.ts gains-bundle-1110 (off vs on jobs per world, bundle sum); hitches only as a no-regression guard. Per-switch ABBA only after a regression. Mint fusion on-arm gate: log 'OK   mintfuse', mfReady 1. Run: node tools/harness/queue.ts tools/harness/queues/gains-bundle-1110.json",
